  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(x=t^{\\frac{1}{t-1}}\\) and \\(y=t^{\\frac{t}{t-1}},\\) \\(t\\gt0,\\) \\(t\\ne1,\\) a relation between \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(y^x=x^{\\frac{1}{y}}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(y^{\\frac{1}{x}}=x^y\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(y^x=x^y\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(x^x=y^y\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1969-p29.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Dividing the definitions gives \\[ \\frac yx=t^{\\frac{t-1}{t-1}}=t. \\] Also, \\[ y=t^{\\frac{t}{t-1}}=\\left(t^{\\frac{1}{t-1}}\\right)^t=x^t. \\] Substituting \\(t=\\frac{y}{x}\\) gives \\(y=x^{\\frac{y}{x}}.\\) Raising both sides to the power \\(x\\) yields \\(y^x=x^y.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Divide \\(y\\) by \\(x\\) to express \\(t\\) in terms of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\)",
        "Also observe that \\(y=x^t\\), then eliminate \\(t\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
